  "_comment": "A night shift in the scrapyard: the intake belt carries the field off the line, into the press hall where three rows of presses slam down in turn, a chicane through tyre stacks and crates, the shaker floor that rolls under the karts, up the scrap heap and a glide off it into the crusher yard, the crane bay with a pallet deck swinging on its chains across the road, and the return belt, running against the traffic until someone pulls the shift lever and sends it the other way. The lever also opens a cut through the breakers' yard, and on the last lap the return belt shakes too.",
